§ `Section 1`

-- One test per element of s 1(1), a test where every element is present, and the two limbs that work through ss 5(2) and 5(4).
#ASSERT `s 1 guilty of theft` `theft all`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 1 guilty of theft` `theft but honest`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 1 guilty of theft` `theft but believed right`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 1 guilty of theft` `theft but no appropriation`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 1 guilty of theft` `theft but not property`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 1 guilty of theft` `theft but nobody else's`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 1 guilty of theft` `theft but no intention to deprive`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 1 guilty of theft` `theft but purchaser`)
#ASSERT `s 1 guilty of theft` `theft of trust property by defeating the trust`
#ASSERT `s 1 guilty of theft` `theft of mistaken payment by not repaying`

-- src:8 | (2) It is immaterial whether the appropriation is made with a view to gain, or is made for the thief’s own benefit.
#ASSERT `s 1 guilty of theft` `theft all` EQUALS `s 1 guilty of theft` `theft all with gain`

§ `Section 2`

#ASSERT `s 2 the appropriation is dishonest` `dis plain`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 2 the appropriation is dishonest` `dis honest`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 2 the appropriation is dishonest` `dis legal right`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 2 the appropriation is dishonest` `dis consent belief`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 2 the appropriation is dishonest` `dis owner unfindable`)
#ASSERT `s 2 the appropriation is dishonest` `dis owner unfindable trustee`
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the appropriation is not to be regarded as dishonest` `dis legal right`
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the appropriation is not to be regarded as dishonest` `dis consent belief`
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the appropriation is not to be regarded as dishonest` `dis owner unfindable`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 2(1) the appropriation is not to be regarded as dishonest` `dis owner unfindable trustee`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 2(1) the appropriation is not to be regarded as dishonest` `dis plain`)

-- src:15 | (2) A person’s appropriation of property belonging to another may be dishonest notwithstanding that he is willing to pay for the property.
#ASSERT `s 2 the appropriation is dishonest` `dis plain willing`
#ASSERT `s 2 the appropriation is dishonest` `dis plain` EQUALS `s 2 the appropriation is dishonest` `dis plain willing`
#ASSERT `s 2 the appropriation is dishonest` `dis legal right` EQUALS `s 2 the appropriation is dishonest` `dis legal right willing`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 2 the appropriation is dishonest` `dis honest willing`)

§ `Section 3`

#ASSERT `s 3(1) he appropriates` `app assumed`
#ASSERT `s 3(1) he appropriates` `app later`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3(1) he appropriates` `app later but came by it by stealing`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3(1) he appropriates` `app came by it innocently only`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3(1) he appropriates` `app none`)
#ASSERT `s 3 he appropriates, and the appropriation can amount to theft` `app assumed`
#ASSERT `s 3 he appropriates, and the appropriation can amount to theft` `app later`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3 he appropriates, and the appropriation can amount to theft` `app none`)
#ASSERT `s 3(2) a defect in the transferor's title is no theft` `app purchaser`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3 he appropriates, and the appropriation can amount to theft` `app purchaser`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3(2) a defect in the transferor's title is no theft` `app purchaser other ground`)
#ASSERT `s 3 he appropriates, and the appropriation can amount to theft` `app purchaser other ground`
#ASSERT `s 3 he appropriates, and the appropriation can amount to theft` `app purchaser bad faith`
#ASSERT `s 3 he appropriates, and the appropriation can amount to theft` `app purchaser not for value`
#ASSERT `s 3 he appropriates, and the appropriation can amount to theft` `app purchaser beyond rights acquired`

